<%#
  A group's files as a table — the list view's rendering for exactly the rows _file_tile.html.erb
  draws as tiles (Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Row), wherever they come from: a folder section,
  Loose, Backups, Linked, or Generated. `.table` is the shared component (components.css);
  `.project-files` carries only this page's column widths/drops (pages/projects.css), the same
  split files/_list.html.erb's `table.files` makes.

  `row.section` is precomputed by whoever built the row (Maker::ProjectFolderListing for a folder
  row, ProjectsController#show for a Linked one) — this partial never walks the tree itself. Blank
  reads as "Loose", the sweep's own name for the folder's root.

  THE ROW CARRIES THE TILE'S RIGHT-CLICK MENU (stage 4, S4-1) — `file_menu_data`, the one builder
  _file_tile.html.erb uses, emitted on the `<tr>` through `tag.tr` so a nil addon origin is DROPPED
  rather than rendered as `data-addon-open-url=""` (FilesHelper's own rule). Switching to List used
  to lose Note, Download and "Edit in <Addon>" silently; filemenu_controller.js#open reads `href`
  off the cell or its first `<a>`, so Open lands where the name links with no controller change.

  THE NAME OPENS THE FILE (file_path), the same target as _file_tile.html.erb's link, so Tiles and
  List agree about where a file opens from the hub — and how: a click opens it, a double-click
  opens it in a new tab (FilesHelper#file_open_data, on the link; the menu stays on the `<tr>`).

  ORIGIN READS @addon_origins, THE SAME HASH EVERY TILE ON THIS PAGE ALREADY READS FOR ITS
  right-click menu (AddonOrigins#addon_origins_for, one Registry lookup for the whole page) — never
  a second resolution here. A row with no addon origin answers nil and the cell reads "—"; a
  Generated row's origin is never nil, by construction (Maker::AddonOrigin.for is what put it in
  @generated in the first place). The label is parsed rather than re-derived because nothing renders
  the bare addon title today outside this cell — see AddonOrigins' own comment on why `title` isn't
  a key in that hash.

  A LINKED ROW KEEPS ITS TWO CONTROLS (2026-11-02, the UX audit's C8): Detach and Move into
  project, the tile's corner (projects/_linked_actions), in an actions column that renders only
  when a row here is Linked — switching the panel to List used to drop both, leaving a Linked file
  with no way to act on it from the hub. Optional local `notes` ({ node_id => sentence }) puts the
  tile's one-line note under the name here too.
%>
<% notes = local_assigns.fetch(:notes, {}) %>
<% actions = rows.any?(&:linked?) %>
<table class="table project-files">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th class="col-name">Name</th>
      <th class="col-section">Section</th>
      <th class="num col-size">Size</th>
      <th class="col-modified">Modified</th>
      <th class="col-origin">Origin</th>
      <% if actions %><th class="col-actions"><span class="label-hidden">Actions</span></th><% end %>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <% rows.each do |row| %>
      <% node = row.node %>
      <% origin = @addon_origins[row.node_id] %>
      <%= tag.tr(data: file_menu_data(node, origin)) do %>
        <td class="col-name">
          <%= link_to node.name, file_path(row.node_id), data: file_open_data %>
          <% if (note = notes[row.node_id]) %><span class="row-note muted"><%= note %></span><% end %>
        </td>
        <td class="muted col-section"><%= row.section.presence || "Loose" %></td>
        <td class="num muted col-size"><%= node.size ? number_to_human_size(node.size) : "—" %></td>
        <td class="muted col-modified">
          <%= node.mtime ? time_at(time_from_nanos(node.mtime)) : "—" %>
        </td>
        <td class="muted col-origin"><%= origin ? origin[:title] : "—" %></td>
        <% if actions %>
          <td class="col-actions"><%= render "projects/linked_actions", row: row, node: node, tile: false %></td>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>
